    "api_error_status": null,
    "result": "`encode` and `decode` are implemented in `solution.py`, and all 24 tests in `tests/test_solution.py` pass with `python -m pytest -q tests`. I didn't measure line coverage. Every branch of both functions is exercised, so I expect it to clear the 90% gate.\n\n`encode` writes each maximal run of four or more as `~n~c`. It escapes shorter runs of `~` as `~~` and leaves other short runs as they are. `decode` raises `ValueError` for each malformed case in the spec: a trailing `~`, a bad character after `~`, leading zeros, a count below 4, a missing closing `~`, and a missing character after it. It also accepts well-formed text that `encode` wouldn't produce, such as plain `\"aaaa\"`.\n\nThe tests cover fixed encode and decode examples, the lenient decode cases, each error case, and a round-trip check over all strings up to length 6 on the alphabet `a`, `~` and `1`.",
